 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The web process uses the shared `sessions` instance from
+[`larder/session_store.py`](../../larder/session_store.py), following the decision to
+[keep sessions in process memory](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Sessions disappear on process restart or deploy, including sessions previously stored in Postgres. Members must
+  sign in again after the switch and after restarts.
+- Each process has its own sessions. A request reaching another process cannot find the member's session. Route a
+  member's requests to the same process to avoid these misses; this does not preserve sessions across restarts.
+- The store does not evict entries or enforce expiry. Callers must enforce the lifetime above; memory remains
+  allocated until a session is replaced or the process restarts.
 
 ## Shaped by
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- [Keep sessions in process memory](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md)
